# One extractor, worked, refreshed, and worked again - twelve food from a deposit of six.
#
# **The extractor is spent inside the test rather than in the `given`.** It was the other way
# round, and the mutation check said the `given` could have started it ready and the test would
# still have passed - so it showed that refresh and work compose, not that refresh was needed.
#
# **Now every line of the `given` is load-bearing.** Starting at `working:0` refuses the first
# work; deleting the refresh refuses the second; one labor refuses the second; and the density is
# what makes twelve rather than any other number.
#
# **Found by the quality lens re-deriving the survivor** rather than by a check - the check named
# the row and the reading of why the obvious repair would not have worked was a person's.

{test name:refresh-lets-a-spent-extractor-work-again}

{given}
{territory id:1}
{deposit where:1 what:31 density:6 quantity:1}
{extractor where:1 what:31 working:1 quantity:1}
{labor where:1 quantity:2}

{when}
{work where:1 what:31}
{refresh what:19 trait:2}
{work where:1 what:31}

{then}
{territory id:1}
{deposit where:1 what:31 density:6 quantity:1}
{extractor where:1 what:31 working:0 quantity:1}
{food where:1 quantity:12}
